    <string name="ui_ec7627907a68" formatted="false">All GPIOs are 3.3 V, not 5 V tolerant. For a confirmed 5 V PWM signal: receiver → 4.7 kΩ → GPIO, plus 6.8 kΩ from GPIO to ground (1% resistors): about 2.96 V. A 3.3 V signal becomes 1.95 V and may not register. Prefer SN74LVC1G17 at 3.3 V if power sequencing varies. Add 10 kΩ from each ESC output GPIO to ground; optional 100–220 Ω output series resistor only reduces ringing, not voltage.</string>
